wn”) 4 Tajiev (fnu) 114 Tajik 45 transliteration ix, 135(n1) Tajik (word) “accepted explanation of origin” 4 “first recorded use” 3–4 Tajik Alphabet Committee 81 Tajik ASSR see Tajik Autonomous Soviet Socialist Republic Tajik ASSR: Central Executive Committee (TsIK) 56, 61, 114, 117 Tajik ASSR: Congress of Soviets 114, 115, 117\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA Spectacle of Maps: Cartographic Hopes and Anxieties in the Pamirs (https://epub.ub.uni-muenchen.de/41861/1/Martin_Saxer_A_Spectacle_of_Maps_Cartographic_hopes.pdf)\nciteturn282search15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 9.8 years ago; Crawled: 8.8 years ago; \nThe western part of the Pamirs had faced quite a different fate. After the 1895 Anglo-Russian border agreement, the districts of Rushan, Shughnan, Ishkashim, and Wakhan had been allocated to the Russian sphere of influence, and its administration was handed over to the Amir of Bukhara. This led to considerable grievances in the region, as the Amir regarded the predominantly Shia Ismai’li population as heretics. Alarming reports by two commanders of the Russian frontier detachment at the beginning of the twentieth century led to an official investigation of Bukharan misrule and finally to direct “temporary Russian administration,” which allowed the local population a limited amount of self-rule. After the revolution, however, this temporary special status was abandoned and the Western Pamirs were integrated into the Bukharan People’s Soviet Republic, the successor state of the Emirate of Bukhara (Bergne 2007, 33–34). In the context of the National-Territorial Delimitation, the Eastern and Western Pamirs were merged into the newly founded Gorno-Badakhshan Autonomous Region (Gorno-Badakhshanskaya avtonomnaya oblast’, or GBAO) and incorporated into the Tajik Autonomous Soviet Socialist Republic, which was initially part of the Uzbek Soviet Socialist Republic and was subsequently promoted to the status of a Soviet Socialist Republic (SSR) in October 1929 (Bergne 2007, 1).\n\nThis brief summary of the admittedly much more complex cartographic process of National-Territorial Delimitation has to suffice here for the argument I seek to make: namely, that internal border delimitation in Soviet Asia corresponds to a kind of cartographic anxiety quite different from the one that infused Great Game politics. Rather than being concerned with\n\nCross-Currents: East Asian History and Culture Review  \nE-Journal No. 21 (December 2016) • (http://cross-currents.berkeley.edu/e-journal/issue-21)--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n〖ジャンクヤード〗Twitter（X）海まとめ321-10：社会・犯罪・政治｜三宅つの (https://note.com/xnbmlbxkkl/n/n3f65914fb76c)\nciteturn282search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.6 years ago; Crawled: yesterday; \n> \n> — ぐらーく (@Gulag1209) March 7, 2025\n\n> 🇺🇸「日本の指導者に通貨を切り下げてはならないと伝えた」\n> 🇯🇵「知らん…何それ…怖…」\n> 🇺🇸「ゼレンスキー大統領から書簡を受け取った」\n> 🇺🇦「知らん…何それ…怖…」\n> 🇺🇸「イランに核交渉の書簡を送った」\n> 🇮🇷「知らん…何それ…怖…」 https://t.co/gYuSc86EPf\n> \n> — フォン・アカリーフェン (@Akalieffen_Plan) March 8, 2025\n\n> アメリカ人の半数はまだ「次の選挙でアメリカは元に戻る」と思ってたりするんだろうけど、共和党が今のままMAGA党である限り、もはやアメリカは元には戻らないよね。てか、我々外国人はそれを前提にして今後のこと考えるしかないよね、残念ながら。\n> \n> — 堺三保/Mitsuyasu Sakai (@Sakai_Sampo) March 7, 2025\n\n> マスクがスターリンクの使用をめぐってポーランド外相を口汚く罵倒した件でフォローに入ったルビオが「スターリンクにも感謝しましょう」と述べたことに対し、ポーランドは米国の一民間企業のサービスを定価で購入して宇軍に使わせているという話なのに何で「感謝」？という妥当なツッコミ https://t.co/7jOGSHzjh8\n> \n> — 露探〖円谷猪四郎〗 (@karategin) March 9, 2025\n\n> あれは皮肉の積りで作った動画だったのに当事者が大喜びしたっていうギャグ漫画みたいな展開だったの・・・ https://t.co/YMFSnW9OHw\n> \n> — JSF (@rockfish31) March 10, 2025\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPeople's cyclopedia;a complete library of reference containing the exact knowledge of the world condensed to the plainest terms consistent with accuracy and clearness, (Vol. 5, Theo-Zym, Appendix) (https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a0/Books_from_the_Library_of_Congress_%28IA_peoplescyclopedi05unse